  "title": "Group laws that compose like cycles keep their top rigid",
  "subject": "Which group laws compose like cycles, and what their global failures keep",
  "conclusion": "A group's coset law composes like cycles exactly when every subgroup has a unique maximal normal subgroup (18 non-abelian such groups up to order 60), and its knots are pulled back from cyclic p-group relations. For systems with declared domains the top image after any removal from a global failure is at most one line; the law is rigid at prime-order sections, and C5:C4 and D9 keep knots below the top.",
